{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview","id":1111834,"title":"The True Fae [New Changeling Second Edition preview]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-05T15:23:00-07:00","id":1111834,"title":"The True Fae [New Changeling Second Edition preview]","content":"Here they are in all their unholy glory<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-true-fae-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-true-fae-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\"> The True Fae [Changeling: The Lost] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-true-fae-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/the-true-fae-changeling-the-lost/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T15:32:37-07:00","id":1111841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview#post1111834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here they are in all their unholy glory<br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-true-fae-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-true-fae-...ling-the-lost/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Glorious indeed. To the writers, kudos: every time I think I could not get more hyped for 2nd Edition, you release a new update that proves me wrong","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T16:52:50-07:00","id":1111888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1111841#post1111841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glorious indeed. To the writers, kudos: every time I think I could not get more hyped for 2nd Edition, you release a new update that proves me wrong</div> </div> </div> </div>I had my concerns, but I've gotta admit, I'm looking forward to seeing the final product in all its glory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T16:58:06-07:00","id":1111891,"title":"","content":"There is <i>a lot</i> that was cool and memorable from Equinox Road in this, and a lot that just gets to the heart of the existence of the True Fae and delves even deeper into it, and I love it.<br /> <br /> The nitty-gritty has some bits of opaque comprehension because we still don't know exactly how Regalia function, and it's still a preview, but it makes them look very impressive. I'm not yet grasping the interplay between their Name, Titles and all their oaths and contracts, but the preview paints a fascinating picture between those parts.<br /> <br /> There are a few details nagging me, but they may turn out to be no concern at all. Particular advantages or benefits the Gentry gain from coining Contracts and some other kinds of promises seem elusive despite their significant importance, but my confusion may just be because of missing context. I'm somewhat confused why they're barred from having Kiths, or even only the benefits of a Kith bereft of the significance they have for changelings, when they're even able to claim the trappings and blessings of Seemings. It seems to close a lot of space for innate abilities or features of their mien that many of their manifestations ought to have.<br /> <br /> The example True Fae in the 1,001 Stories section are all disturbingly terrific, but the lines that mention their Changelings seem to imply Seeming is again something the Keeper shapes a Changeling into rather than something the Lost make for themselves in reclaiming their freedom. Maybe I'm misreading the wording.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-05-2017, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T17:30:15-07:00","id":1111901,"title":"","content":"I don't think you're misreading it. A new team of writers rewrote everything that had previously been done and put out as spoilers. I expect we're back to hope things worked in 1ed in regards to seeming/kiths, static courts, and everything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T18:09:04-07:00","id":1111915,"title":"","content":"We already know Courts aren't exactly like in first edition, in both unbent assumptions and the practical form of their essential contributions to Changeling society, so that doesn't quite hold. The Seasonal Courts are presented upfront as a recognizable option, but the book is still set to include a section to create your own courts and freehold, while the settings chapter is supposed to include quite a few distinct and very different courts from all over the world. Huntsmen are also new and they're still in, though we don't know how their rules may have changed.<br /> <br /> To be blunt about my meaning, I hope I'm misreading the section at hand because the reconceptualized Seemings as originally previewed were incredibly compelling material, and it would be a shame to lose it for something closer to the First Edition Seemings.<br /> <br /> (I doubt this last thing would be the case even if the concept in the Second Edition core has been extensively rewritten, but I digress.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-05-2017, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T18:15:26-07:00","id":1111919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1111901#post1111901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you're misreading it. A new team of writers rewrote everything that had previously been done and put out as spoilers. I expect we're back to hope things worked in 1ed in regards to seeming/kiths, static courts, and everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes I loved how the vast majority of the True Fae stuff was done, I'm curious what the Eidolons are, BUT if they git rid of the David Hill's kiths and seemings I'll be devastated, they had such depth, such insight into humanity, and what shapes and empowers us and it was plain and simply amazing that to lose that would be very upsetting honestly. The Darkling in particular really connected with me on a deep level. <br /> <br /> So mixed feelings here, True Fae are badass, yet thematic, scary enough to worry a pack of Werewolves, or a Master Mage, but with potential vulneriblies that could make it possible for even a lucky or clever or well informed Hunter to beat one. Many other things were teased at that have me intrigued and worth discussing, but the loss of David's Kith/Seemings is deeply, deeply disappointing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T18:20:38-07:00","id":1111921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1111915#post1111915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be blunt about my meaning, I hope I'm misreading the section at hand because the reconceptualized Seemings as originally previewed were incredibly compelling material.</div> </div> </div> </div> that is my feeling as well, I think if it has been changed it will not be a popular one, as I think that was one of the most popular things, if not THE most popular thing David Hill did for Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T18:45:45-07:00","id":1111930,"title":"","content":"Bits from Grandmother, Grandmother's entry in particular seem almost <i>conflicted</i> on whether or not Seemings are still agency-related. In one line, it describes her actively (if perhaps not consciously) sculpting changelings into defined Seemings, but later goes on to describe escape opportunities in a manner where the three example Seemings almost blatantly adhere to the previous design.<br /> <br /> The preview at large certainly makes the Gentry feel rather impressive, don't get me wrong; I'm already starting to think of ideas for how to use what we've gotten here to interesting effect. But due in part to the above, I can't help but feel confused and concerned, which distracts me a little from the good aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 07-05-2017, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T18:57:10-07:00","id":1111931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1111930#post1111930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bits from Grandmother, Grandmother's entry in particular seem almost <i>conflicted</i> on whether or not Seemings are still agency-related. In one line, it describes her actively (if perhaps not consciously) sculpting changelings into defined Seemings, but later goes on to describe escape opportunities in a manner where the three example Seemings almost blatantly adhere to the previous design.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guess errata phase is going to be fun if this particular bit isn't already fixed when heading out in Advance PDF form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T19:23:41-07:00","id":1111942,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of great stuff here; First edition I felt like I had to read a couple of splat books to get a handle on what the True Fae really were and how they worked, and it really feels like all of that was condensed into this one section. Mechanically it looks like Equinox Road but a bit more streamlined, and I was always a fan of the scaling power level Titles allowed for, where a one Title Fae was powerful but not unbeatable and a five Title was a terrifying end boss. I'm glad they kept that.<br /> <br /> I'm less enamored with their complete immunity to non bane damage. I get that injuring a Fae needs to be a big deal, and it certainly does incentivize seeking out their weaknesses rather than attempting to brute force the problem with More Dakka, but it negates the classic &quot;Lure the nearly invincible monster into massive environmental damage&quot; trope. It narrows the range of creative options in a way I find restrictive. Maybe if Titles also granted armor against all non bane sources instead of flat immunity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T20:10:55-07:00","id":1111959,"title":"","content":"I also read the bits about Seemings in a very 1e light, and Grandmother, Grandmother is very conflicted on which is which, but to me (rereading with a 2e lens in mind) it seems almost like the writeup is suggesting that with the roles in the &quot;family&quot; Grandmother, Grandmother favours, the True Fae is trying to <i>push </i>Changelings to escape in certain ways.<br /> <br /> In regards to hurting the Gentry, it says they don't take damage from anything except Banes, which, at Wyrd 5 minimum, they're guaranteed to have at least <i>one </i>of. Iron deals Lethal damage, and Cold Iron deals Aggravated damage. However, it also adds the little wrinkle of if you know the Gentry's Name (fairly certain this is their True Name, which isn't really comprehensible unless they are without Title) <i>then </i>you can inflict Lethal damage if you incorporate it as part of the attack. The True Fae as written here remind me a lot of the Rakshasa from Exalted Second Edition, especially with how True Fae Regalia (possibly all Regalia?) require physical touchstones and how Titles correlate to Regalia. I wouldn't mind some guidelines regarding how to represent Titles that are <i>not </i>presenting as Actors though, guidelines for how Title-as-Realm or Title-as-Wisp or Title-as-Prop would look.<br /> <br /> Also, that line about the Gentry finding the barrows of the beings that would become the Huntsmen? Chills. If there's one trope that I really always adore, it's the idea of Things Before, things ancient and unfathomable that should have been left alone. The Gentry rule now, but the things that became Huntsmen were rulers of Arcadia once, and I'm eager to see what Huntsmen are like now in order to get an idea of what they were made from.<br /> <br /> Things that I really enjoy:<ul><li>The True Fae feel impressive and godlike, but not totally insurmountable anymore than a Rank 5 Ephemeral Being is insurmountable though it is still impressive and godlike</li> <li>The True Fae feel like twisted reflections of the Lost, Changelings without their &quot;vulnerabilities&quot; like Clarity. Without Clarity, the Gentry have absolutely no compunction about doing whatever they need to, can Embrace the Wyrd all they want, and can Reap Glamour all they want.</li> <li>The True Fae don't have Anchors. They don't have a Virtue, Vice, Touchstones, or any equivalents. Their means of regaining Willpower? Aspirations. The only means of <i>retaining </i>Willpower past a scene? Aspirations pertaining to stealing mortals or conflicting with Changelings. If the mind of a mortal or mortal-like character can be said to be rooted in their Virtue and Vice or equivalent, then the Gentry are perhaps more alien than anything except Spirits because they <i>are </i>their desires and whims. To feel fulfilled and whole, they need to constantly chase those desires, and the only way they will ever <i>really </i>be &quot;satisfied&quot; is by possessing power over mortals, and <i>that </i>scares the hell out of me.</li> <li>I like that there's a &quot;when the stars are right&quot; option for the Gentry. Even if killed, even if their Name is shattered and their Titles stripped, if those Titles live on in another character, perhaps one day the True Fae that originally possessed them will return.</li> <li>The Gentry can treat the entire world outside of Ironside like a dream. That is thematic, awesome, and lets them do a lot of very cool abstract things on par with Influences (at least if the dream shaping rules are relatively unchanged). I'm not entirely sure how this impacts Hedge shaping, if that's still a thing, unless Hedge spinning covers what was called Hedge shaping in the previous previews in addition to what we normally think of a Hedge spinning.</li> <li>The Gentry have power over Names that makes them a frightening prospect to deal with, and which can make abducting someone almost trivially easy. However, this works in to the way the Gentry handle Pledges in a way that seems super cool. The Gentry place no value on their word, what they say and what they feel (even though desire and whim define their personality), they place value on their possessions. As an aside, it looks like the Game of Immortals from Equinox Road is still present in the sense that the best way to kill a True Fae and/or gain a Title is to trap it in a web of Pledges it can't uphold.</li> <li>Between Glamour addiction, and how lessened their considerable powers are in Ironside, it looks like luring a True Fae to earth is the best way to kick its teeth in. Get some mortals or Fae-Touched you trust, load them up with Cold Iron, and have at 'em.</li> </ul><br /> The thing that concern me:<ul><li>The True Fae get an imitation Seeming but no Kiths? That worries me a lot. It feels very 1e, and even if the pseudo-Seeming is only to gain the Regalia affinity it grants, it still seems very odd and almost... wrong to have the Gentry just as a matter of their nature have something that is rooted in agency and reclamation of self for the Lost. Kiths make much more sense, roles that the Gentry take up willingly but that they force on their captives. Then you would get something rather like the 1e suggestions of Seemings and Kiths favoured by certain Keepers, except it would just be Kiths- the Kiths they themselves possess. Who knows, maybe some Gentry like to use Kiths that compliment or contrast their own.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T08:25:21-07:00","id":1112118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1111959#post1111959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The True Fae feel like twisted reflections of the Lost, Changelings without their &quot;vulnerabilities&quot; like Clarity. Without Clarity, the Gentry have absolutely no compunction about doing whatever they need to, can Embrace the Wyrd all they want, and can Reap Glamour all they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>The True Fae's lack of Clarity says some interesting things about them. Clarity, in second edition, is about owning your own perceptions, knowing your own truth. As a changeling, you always see both the mortal and faerie worlds. The powers of both those worlds tell you that their &quot;side&quot; is the only one that matters, the only one that's real, and you say &quot;no, I know what I see and where I've been, I know who I am.&quot;<br /> <br /> The True Fae don't have that. The world-shaping power of their own will blinds them to realities they don't control, that aren't part of their web of agreements and illusions. Rather than knowing their own truth, they force their whims to act like truth.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T08:46:54-07:00","id":1112127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112118#post1112118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The True Fae's lack of Clarity says some interesting things about them. Clarity, in second edition, is about owning your own perceptions, knowing your own truth. As a changeling, you always see both the mortal and faerie worlds. The powers of both those worlds tell you that their &quot;side&quot; is the only one that matters, the only one that's real, and you say &quot;no, I know what I see and where I've been, I know who I am.&quot;<br /> <br /> The True Fae don't have that. The world-shaping power of their own will blinds them to realities they don't control, that aren't part of their web of agreements and illusions. Rather than knowing their own truth, they force their whims to act like truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deep stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T09:20:38-07:00","id":1112145,"title":"","content":"It's the Abuse Metaphor In the core of changeling. An abuser tries to gaslight you,to make you believe in whatever he wants you to with no regard for you and tey refuse to see the truth,especially the truth that they are indeed abusers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T09:46:12-07:00","id":1112162,"title":"","content":"Since devs are in the thread, can I ask if there is still room for Seemings as what you did to escape? Even before 2e, there were Characters like Calamity the Darkling Razorhand from the Malibu Dream House actual play who gained their kith and maybe even Seeming not just from what their Keeper did to them, but from the bargains and methods they used to escape (Calamity merged with the Glass she used to carve a way out of the giant snowglobe town she was stuck in). Changeling are already so defined by what was done to them that it was really rewarding to see one way to reflect how you used your own sense of identity to gain the power to break free. Now all the categories you use to define yourself are tied to what something else made you into.<br /> <br /> Edit: OK, there's still Courts and Entitlements for Chosen fae categories, but they don't have the same visceral quality that having the Wyrd itself grant you a new form and powers did. Plus, there's gotta be more fairytale roles than hero, damsel, servant, magical animal, villain, prop, the elements of nature or storyteller","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 07-06-2017, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:01:56-07:00","id":1112171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112162#post1112162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since devs are in the thread, can I ask if there is still room for Seemings as what you did to escape?</div> </div> </div> </div>A seeming is made up of three things: the fairy tale role you played in Arcadia, the way you took ownership of that role and turned it against your Keeper to escape, and the way you take advantage of your faerie nature to reclaim your life in the present. The archetype-driven character creation of the Chronicles of Darkness presents these as packages-with-flexibility, but there's fully room for you to handle each element in different ways and say &quot;<i>this</i> is what defines my seeming.&quot; Here's the example I gave in the blog comments:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, an Elemental might be someone who took on the role of a storm. Then, they used their might to smash their way out of Faerie, stranding their Keeper in a downpour while rattling the gates of his domain to pieces with thunder. Now, their friends know that when danger calls for unrelenting persistence and maybe a lightning strike that shorts out a city block, the elemental is the one to have on speed dial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many parts of the setting in 2e have sections for &quot;Then&quot; (describing Arcadia and the escape) and &quot;Now&quot; (talking about how you take your life back in the face of mundane and supernatural challenges alike). The seeming writeups also have &quot;Tales,&quot; paragraph-long example characters showing the lives changelings have built for themselves.<br /> <br /> If possible, could we keep this thread mainly on the True Fae? The feedback is very useful.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112162#post1112162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, there's gotta be more fairytale roles than hero, damsel, servant, magical animal, villain, prop, the elements of nature or storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>There certainly are! More seemings are possible for future books, and I'd even like to get into design-a-seeming in a player's guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 07-06-2017, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:07:14-07:00","id":1112174,"title":"","content":"I love a goood villain. The true fae have been some of my faves. And this new edition seems make them even more complex and cool. the lines some of them being explorers that figured out where the huntsman hide was really greaat,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:13:16-07:00","id":1112175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112171#post1112171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If possible, could we keep this thread mainly on the True Fae? The feedback is very useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Sorry about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112171#post1112171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There certainly are! More seemings are possible for future books, and I'd even like to get into design-a-seeming in a player's guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>You had my attention, but now you have a devoted buyer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 07-06-2017, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:55:51-07:00","id":1112210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112118#post1112118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The True Fae's lack of Clarity says some interesting things about them. Clarity, in second edition, is about owning your own perceptions, knowing your own truth. As a changeling, you always see both the mortal and faerie worlds. The powers of both those worlds tell you that their &quot;side&quot; is the only one that matters, the only one that's real, and you say &quot;no, I know what I see and where I've been, I know who I am.&quot;<br /> <br /> The True Fae don't have that. The world-shaping power of their own will blinds them to realities they don't control, that aren't part of their web of agreements and illusions. Rather than knowing their own truth, they force their whims to act like truth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pictured: A privateer and his master:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://lparchive.org/Earthbound/Update%2032/23-capture_16042008_001948.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T11:03:14-07:00","id":1112224,"title":"","content":"I always liked the idea of the Gentry wanting humans for the exotic taste of Glamour. Being in Arcadia, they have neigh absolute amounts, but it's probably stale or lacking compared to the stuff you can harvest from mortals. The difference between a feast of identical muffins and a single plate of Black Forest g\u00e2teau.<br /> <br /> Edit: Then again, perhaps the Gentry can feed off each other, much like changelings can goblins. Can you imagine what the True Fae must taste like to each other?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 07-06-2017, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T11:21:44-07:00","id":1112234,"title":"","content":"I like it. In 1001 Stories, the addressing of Gentry and Seeming interaction reinforces the major elements of a Seeming. Obviously, this is not the section I would expect to see how anything but the Gentry would affect Seeming development. I wouldn't say I needed the examples, but I find them obligatory and I like different sections to reinforce each other. The actual Keepers were unique. I would not have thought of them.<br /> <br /> I know nothing of Regalia so I can't speak to how that works with the True Fae. I appreciate names, titles, and pacts. I'm not sure about the damaging of Gentry. My first thought was they sound like cartoon characters. It might work as far as game, but an example leading to me away from cartoons would have been nice.<br /> <br /> Makes sense to me for a True Fae not to have a kith. Kiths are specialized and suggest a rigidity that I don't expect from a True Fae. A Seeming is more of a general role (leader, brute, sneak, specialist, savage, and force of nature by my reckoning) so a Title should more of less have something like a Seeming since it is also a role. If True Fae had kiths then I would be wondering what do they have Changelings for? Also, True Fae with fluid kiths sounds like a drag to me, that being the only way it would make any sense to me for a True Fae to have a kith.<br /> <br /> Questions:<br /> <br /> Aspirations can be fulfilled repeated but no mention of how often. How often can Willpower be regained? I'm not sure if the True Fae have a hard time or not of it or not.<br /> <br /> How rigid is a Title's appearance? The text isn't clear to me if Titles can have vastly different appearances or do. Could a sorceress turn into a dragon without it being different Titles? Probably a bad example but it was the first thing that popped into my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T12:19:25-07:00","id":1112265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112234#post1112234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How rigid is a Title's appearance? The text isn't clear to me if Titles can have vastly different appearances or do. Could a sorceress turn into a dragon without it being different Titles? Probably a bad example but it was the first thing that popped into my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Title can manifest in many different ways--it can pretty much change form at will, as long as its tell is still present one way or another, and it still embodies the general themes of the Title. So Maleficent (which is what your example made me think of <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) is perfectly doable as a True Fae Title that embodies ruthlessness, jealousy, and green fire. (As a completely off the cuff for-instance.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T12:26:48-07:00","id":1112271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112265#post1112265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Title can manifest in many different ways--it can pretty much change form at will, as long as its tell is still present one way or another, and it still embodies the general themes of the Title. So Maleficent (which is what your example made me think of <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) is perfectly doable as a True Fae Title that embodies ruthlessness, jealousy, and green fire. (As a completely off the cuff for-instance.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Fascinating","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T12:35:37-07:00","id":1112273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112265#post1112265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Title can manifest in many different ways--it can pretty much change form at will, as long as its tell is still present one way or another, and it still embodies the general themes of the Title. So Maleficent (which is what your example made me think of <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) is perfectly doable as a True Fae Title that embodies ruthlessness, jealousy, and green fire. (As a completely off the cuff for-instance.)</div> </div> </div> </div> So, would Maelifcent be the True Name, and Mistress of All Evil be the Title?<br /> <br /> <br /> I want to do her as a Keeper in my game now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> &lt;3 Maleficent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112234#post1112234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How rigid is a Title's appearance? The text isn't clear to me if Titles can have vastly different appearances or do. Could a sorceress turn into a dragon without it being different Titles? Probably a bad example but it was the first thing that popped into my head.</div> </div> </div> </div> At the very least, even if a Title has a single &quot;appearance&quot; (an ill fitting word, considering that Titles can take the form of the land itself, a hoard of fae beings, and magic items), one would still have access to Contracts. Maleficent turning into a dragon could just be a natural ability, or it could be a use of Chrysalis, for instance. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-06-2017, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T13:19:10-07:00","id":1112300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112210#post1112210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Pictured: A privateer and his master:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>All my nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T13:20:32-07:00","id":1112302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112118#post1112118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The True Fae's lack of Clarity says some interesting things about them. Clarity, in second edition, is about owning your own perceptions, knowing your own truth. As a changeling, you always see both the mortal and faerie worlds. The powers of both those worlds tell you that their &quot;side&quot; is the only one that matters, the only one that's real, and you say &quot;no, I know what I see and where I've been, I know who I am.&quot;<br /> <br /> The True Fae don't have that. The world-shaping power of their own will blinds them to realities they don't control, that aren't part of their web of agreements and illusions. Rather than knowing their own truth, they force their whims to act like truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lovely irony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T13:29:26-07:00","id":1112309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112265#post1112265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Title can manifest in many different ways--it can pretty much change form at will, as long as its tell is still present one way or another, and it still embodies the general themes of the Title. So Maleficent (which is what your example made me think of <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) is perfectly doable as a True Fae Title that embodies ruthlessness, jealousy, and green fire. (As a completely off the cuff for-instance.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thank you. Maleficent was indeed my example. She was the first thing that I thought of when reading about Title manifestations. You are better than me to come up with a Title that could match those manifestations. I read it as you say. I wanted to make sure that I had it right as the Name and Title distinction can be complex. Very nice. I actually love that, extremely powerful narrative tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T14:00:37-07:00","id":1112329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112309#post1112309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, thank you. Maleficent was indeed my example. She was the first thing that I thought of when reading about Title manifestations. You are better than me to come up with a Title that could match those manifestations. I read it as you say. I wanted to make sure that I had it right as the Name and Title distinction can be complex. Very nice. I actually love that, extremely powerful narrative tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>What of, say, Sheogorath?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T14:41:16-07:00","id":1112351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112