 href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T14:51:30-07:00","id":1112359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112354#post1112354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that is rather the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well remember: Sheogorath avoids having there be TOO much madness in his realm. He says as much in Skyrim. Hence why he has to return, else Haskill gets into too much trouble.<br /> <br /> Perhaps that's a clause in the contract. There has to be some modicum of order, or recognizable pattern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 07-06-2017, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T14:56:50-07:00","id":1112361,"title":"","content":"It sounds like True Fae have no objectivity.<br /> <br /> A 5 titled True Fae will have 50 ability dots, 50 skill dots, and 20 merits, 10 Wyrd, 5 title manifestations, 5 Regalia, the ability to shape shift to almoat anything with a connection to a title, normally doesn't take damage outside specific situations, and you need to get it to break the right promise before you can permantantly kill it or destroy one of its titles, but even then it has the chance to come back to life if any of its passed titles still exists.<br /> <br /> That is one scary foe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T15:07:27-07:00","id":1112364,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A Keeper should scare a Changeling to the point that they would be willing to sell out someone else to their Keeper knowing exactly what horrors the person will face. </span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112361#post1112361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A 5 titled True Fae will have 50 ability dots, 50 skill dots, and 20 merits, 10 Wyrd, 5 title manifestations, 5 Regalia, the ability to shape shift to almoat anything with a connection to a title, normally doesn't take damage outside specific situations, and you need to get it to break the right promise before you can permantantly kill it or destroy one of its titles, but even then it has the chance to come back to life if any of its passed titles still exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'll do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T15:51:46-07:00","id":1112386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112361#post1112361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like True Fae have no objectivity.<br /> <br /> A 5 titled True Fae will have 50 ability dots, 50 skill dots, and 20 merits, 10 Wyrd, 5 title manifestations, 5 Regalia, the ability to shape shift to almoat anything with a connection to a title, normally doesn't take damage outside specific situations, and you need to get it to break the right promise before you can permantantly kill it or destroy one of its titles, but even then it has the chance to come back to life if any of its passed titles still exists.<br /> <br /> That is one scary foe.</div> </div> </div> </div>A worthy challenge, and an excellent end game opponent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T16:01:17-07:00","id":1112391,"title":"","content":"Personnaly I think I would treat the mightiest of the Fae as Death Stars. You don't fight them, you go on epic quests to get their banes (which in true Chronicles of Darkness fashion should actually be rarer but more potent), you persuade them to play a transformation contest where you lure them to shift into three drops of water or something like that, you pledge to accomplish some great task for a letter of their true name.<br /> <br /> A 5 titles fae is a chronicle in itself or at least several scenarios before the climax.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T16:05:33-07:00","id":1112392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112391#post1112391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personnaly I think I would treat the mightiest of the Fae as Death Stars. You don't fight them, you go on epic quests to get their banes (which in true Chronicles of Darkness fashion should actually be rarer but more potent), you persuade them to play a transformation contest where you lure them to shift into three drops of water or something like that, you pledge to accomplish some great task for a letter of their true name.<br /> <br /> A 5 titles fae is a chronicle in itself or at least several scenarios before the climax.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how the strix and idigam work too. Except with something else instead of the transformation contest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T16:12:51-07:00","id":1112398,"title":"","content":"One question I'd like to ask: how long can a motley last inside a Gentry's realm? I know time's dilated, but could you theoretically have a scenario where you have to spend days or even weeks inside enemy territory?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T17:32:59-07:00","id":1112427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112398#post1112398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question I'd like to ask: how long can a motley last inside a Gentry's realm? I know time's dilated, but could you theoretically have a scenario where you have to spend days or even weeks inside enemy territory?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As long as you know the rules and how to exploit them, I would imagine you could spend as long as you want.<br /> <br /> It would be extremely stupid to overstay your welcome. But it's possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T18:02:09-07:00","id":1112436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112398#post1112398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question I'd like to ask: how long can a motley last inside a Gentry's realm? I know time's dilated, but could you theoretically have a scenario where you have to spend days or even weeks inside enemy territory?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no hard limit. The True Fae have many ways of spying out information in their own realms, but don't possess actual omniscience, so avoiding capture is fully viable. Other kinds of survival depend on how hostile the Other has made the place, but since most Keepers' realms present themselves as places human beings can live, you could make it a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T18:11:52-07:00","id":1112439,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there a rule of the Wyrd described in 1e that said all realms had to have some modicum of accommodation to human needs, like something to breathe, something to eat, etc? is that still around?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T18:13:18-07:00","id":1112440,"title":"","content":"Just forget it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 07-06-2017, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T18:21:03-07:00","id":1112441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112439#post1112439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a rule of the Wyrd described in 1e that said all realms had to have some modicum of accommodation to human needs, like something to breathe, something to eat, etc? is that still around?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes there was in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 07-06-2017, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T18:31:31-07:00","id":1112445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112439#post1112439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a rule of the Wyrd described in 1e that said all realms had to have some modicum of accommodation to human needs, like something to breathe, something to eat, etc? is that still around?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Law of Hospitality, I think it was called. Only applied to visitors, not slaves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T20:08:38-07:00","id":1112472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112439#post1112439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a rule of the Wyrd described in 1e that said all realms had to have some modicum of accommodation to human needs, like something to breathe, something to eat, etc? is that still around?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Even if that was the case, the True Fae can shape their realm in nearly any conceivable way. They could make a realm where you breathe cake frosting, or some crazy shit like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T20:29:52-07:00","id":1112478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112472#post1112472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Even if that was the case, the True Fae can shape their realm in nearly any conceivable way. They could make a realm where you breathe cake frosting, or some crazy shit like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. If the logic can work in a fucked-up dream, odds are things are like that i at least one corner of Arcadia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T03:56:22-07:00","id":1112590,"title":"","content":"So. Regalia. It sounds like, from the reading, that Wyrd - 4 Regalia, keeping the maximum of 6 that we've seen and heard of elsewhere (with non-standard Regalia being rumors/paranoia than fact).* Or, more simply, one per title + name. Assuming Contracts remain roughly the same format with seeming affinities replaced with Regalia, the True Fae have access to all Contracts with an affinity listing their Regalia, correct? So, someone with Steed would have access to Fang and Talon, Pathfinder, the traverse mirrors ability, and more.<br /> <br /> This has some rather interesting implications. Goblin Contracts don't have Regalia. We haven't seen any Court Contracts, but I would be surprised if they had Regalia too. This seems to suggest that the Gentry, for all their power, actually have access to only Arcadian Contracts. Granted, a Keeper could likely can have access to Arcadian contracts that no changeling has seen before and mimics a Court Contract. But still, quite curious. For as powerful as a True Fae is, there are sharp limitations.<br /> <br /> * New Regalia don't seem to be a boost in power, but rather a way to add new thematic twists to existing Contracts. A regalia of slime, for instance, could yeild a host of slime-based abilities, such as turning into a gelatinous cube, acting like slimer, and some sleezy twists on social powers. Nothing too powerful, but some way to bring in the strange and alien into the game,seems like. probably less useful than the existing six, but handy for very specific antagonists","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-07-2017, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T05:23:01-07:00","id":1112610,"title":"","content":"So, here's a quick question. I was falling back into the Equinox Road version of the Kindly Ones, and thinking in terms of Actors, Props, <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">Realm or Wisp. Upon second reading, it -sounds- like that's not holding true anymore. Props seem to have been replaced by the Regalia manifestations that you can trap one of the Gentry's Titles. Both a person and a castle seem to be manifesting as a result of a Title, as well as all miscelanious figures. <br /> <br /> So, would the Princess of the Red Crowns be her castle, a manifested changeling, and the castle servants all at once, and the hammer she uses to pound in nails be the Regalia's physical manifestation?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T07:01:24-07:00","id":1112651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112610#post1112610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here's a quick question. I was falling back into the Equinox Road version of the Kindly Ones, and thinking in terms of Actors, Props, <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">Realm or Wisp. Upon second reading, it -sounds- like that's not holding true anymore. Props seem to have been replaced by the Regalia manifestations that you can trap one of the Gentry's Titles. Both a person and a castle seem to be manifesting as a result of a Title, as well as all miscelanious figures. <br /> <br /> So, would the Princess of the Red Crowns be her castle, a manifested changeling, and the castle servants all at once, and the hammer she uses to pound in nails be the Regalia's physical manifestation?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> I think that the manifestation could anything, a character, an actual crown, a castle, a planet (not ironside obviously), an army, ect...<br /> <br /> The possessed regalia is still just a token, not a prop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T07:11:55-07:00","id":1112656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112590#post1112590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. Regalia. It sounds like, from the reading, that Wyrd - 4 Regalia, keeping the maximum of 6 that we've seen and heard of elsewhere (with non-standard Regalia being rumors/paranoia than fact).* Or, more simply, one per title + name. Assuming Contracts remain roughly the same format with seeming affinities replaced with Regalia, the True Fae have access to all Contracts with an affinity listing their Regalia, correct? So, someone with Steed would have access to Fang and Talon, Pathfinder, the traverse mirrors ability, and more.<br /> <br /> This has some rather interesting implications. Goblin Contracts don't have Regalia. We haven't seen any Court Contracts, but I would be surprised if they had Regalia too. This seems to suggest that the Gentry, for all their power, actually have access to only Arcadian Contracts. Granted, a Keeper could likely can have access to Arcadian contracts that no changeling has seen before and mimics a Court Contract. But still, quite curious. For as powerful as a True Fae is, there are sharp limitations.<br /> <br /> * New Regalia don't seem to be a boost in power, but rather a way to add new thematic twists to existing Contracts. A regalia of slime, for instance, could yeild a host of slime-based abilities, such as turning into a gelatinous cube, acting like slimer, and some sleezy twists on social powers. Nothing too powerful, but some way to bring in the strange and alien into the game,seems like. probably less useful than the existing six, but handy for very specific antagonists</div> </div> </div> </div> Regalia is exclusive to Arcadian Contracts, Court &amp; Goblin contracts don't fall under Regalia. <br /> <br /> Contracts still have Seeming blessings, at least Arcadian ones do, court might as well, I don't know at this point. But for example the Steed Ragalia would have all it's contracts having a Beast Seeming blessing (with any other seeming blessings depending on the individual contract).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T07:19:56-07:00","id":1112663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112651#post1112651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think that the manifestation could anything, a character, an actual crown, a castle, a planet (not ironside obviously), an army, ect...<br /> <br /> The possessed regalia is still just a token, not a prop.</div> </div> </div> </div> Props were basically glorified tokens in the first place, so I don't see much of a difference there.<br /> <br /> And I get that manifestations can be anything, but here's the part that I'm confused on - it seems like manifestations can be everything at once. That's slightly different. To use the Princess of the Red Crown as an example once again, she seems to be the Princess herself, -and- the castle, -and- some of the servants going by the blog post. But in 1e, you'd have one title for the realm (castle), one title for the princess, and one title for the servants (wisp). Well, one of those titles could be replaced with the Name, but still.<br /> <br /> So, in 2e, all that is one Title. Then the Princess could have other titles - Scourge of the Bleeding Forests, Heart of the Green Sun, Jewel of the Branch of Horai. Each additional title seems to come with new physical characters, new areas to add to the Princess' realm, and new occupants (beasts of the forest, etc).<br /> <br /> Are they all linked? What happens to the castle if the Princess takes a walk into the mortal world and gets stabbed with iron? What happens when the castle is stabbed with iron? Sure, they all reappear, but does the castle take damage? Have health levels too? <br /> <br /> And what parts are Contracts, and what part are the fey itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-07-2017, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:14:14-07:00","id":1112724,"title":"","content":"To really understand how powerful True Fae are we have to know what Oneriomancy and Hedgespinning looks like because True Fae can use them in both Arcadia and the Hedge to an epic godlike degree? <br /> <br /> Also it's hard to tell how powerful a True Fae's regalia is when we don't know how many contracts each Regalia gets? <br /> <br /> Also for shape shifting if a True Far turns into a giant diamond, do they get a durability and hardness rating? <br /> <br /> If a True Fae, say the Lord of Demonic Cheetahs (with 5 titles), takes the form of a super fast Cheetah that smells like Sulfor, then takes that form of a muscle bound Demonic with the claws and spots of a Cheetah, and then takes the form of a super smart biography book about the Lord of the Demonic Cheetahs, can the True Fae redistribute it's 50 attribute points and 50 skill dots to reflect it's new form when ever it changes form? <br /> <br /> And what about size, does a True Fae gain health if it picks a massive size and loses it when it takes the form of a tiny size?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:17:24-07:00","id":1112726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112663#post1112663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Props were basically glorified tokens in the first place, so I don't see much of a difference there.<br /> <br /> And I get that manifestations can be anything, but here's the part that I'm confused on - it seems like manifestations can be everything at once. That's slightly different. To use the Princess of the Red Crown as an example once again, she seems to be the Princess herself, -and- the castle, -and- some of the servants going by the blog post. But in 1e, you'd have one title for the realm (castle), one title for the princess, and one title for the servants (wisp). Well, one of those titles could be replaced with the Name, but still.<br /> <br /> So, in 2e, all that is one Title. Then the Princess could have other titles - Scourge of the Bleeding Forests, Heart of the Green Sun, Jewel of the Branch of Horai. Each additional title seems to come with new physical characters, new areas to add to the Princess' realm, and new occupants (beasts of the forest, etc).<br /> <br /> Are they all linked? What happens to the castle if the Princess takes a walk into the mortal world and gets stabbed with iron? What happens when the castle is stabbed with iron? Sure, they all reappear, but does the castle take damage? Have health levels too? <br /> <br /> And what parts are Contracts, and what part are the fey itself?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well in 2e a True Fae in the form of a Sword vs trapped in a Token of a Sword would be very different things, no body with a lick of sense wants to wield an active True Fae, while using a token with a True Fae trapped inside of it is dangerous, but not an act of madness, as long as you don't wake it, your fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T11:49:28-07:00","id":1112812,"title":"","content":"New question: how many actors can one Gentry have active at the same time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T12:01:09-07:00","id":1112821,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Sorry, posted this before I saw the request to keep the thread on the topic of True Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-07-2017, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T12:02:28-07:00","id":1112824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112812#post1112812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New question: how many actors can one Gentry have active at the same time?</div> </div> </div> </div>As in, how many ways can a Title be expressed Simultaneously?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T12:12:25-07:00","id":1112829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112824#post1112824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As in, how many ways can a Title be expressed Simultaneously?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but more along the lines of how many individual actors can they have operating at once, regardless of title-sharing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T04:40:22-07:00","id":1113183,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a><br /> <br /> I have a question. The only way for a True Fae to retain Willpower is to earn it pursuing a Changeling. Does it apply to non-Keeper Gentry as well? That would put Strangers indifferent to humanity at a disadvantage, and I wondered if that's intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T04:54:10-07:00","id":1113186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1113183#post1113183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a><br /> <br /> I have a question. The only way for a True Fae to retain Willpower is to earn it pursuing a Changeling. Does it apply to non-Keeper Gentry as well? That would put Strangers indifferent to humanity at a disadvantage, and I wondered if that's intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can also retain Willpower if it was &quot;earned pursuing a craving&quot;, so non-keeper's should be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T05:27:08-07:00","id":1113195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112829#post1112829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but more along the lines of how many individual actors can they have operating at once, regardless of title-sharing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, it says they have nearly infinite power within the confines of their title, so my guess is that they can have as many actors as they desire. Which sells home the idea that these Fae are god-like beings when confronted on their own turf. It also explains why it's impossible to truly hurt them outside of stripping them of their title, since their numbers may as well be legion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-08-2017, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T05:45:05-07:00","id":1113199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1113186#post1113186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can also retain Willpower if it was &quot;earned pursuing a craving&quot;, so non-keeper's should be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaand I misread that like a doofus. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T07:43:57-07:00","id":1113242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1112663#post1112663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they all linked? What happens to the castle if the Princess takes a walk into the mortal world and gets stabbed with iron? What happens when the castle is stabbed with iron? Sure, they all reappear, but does the castle take damage? Have health levels too?<br /> <br /> And what parts are Contracts, and what part are the fey itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the entire thing -is- the fey Title. They'll all take health levels in damage, or structural/durability damage if they're a structure or an object. But they'll call come back with no long term harm: they're all essentially expressions of Contract, because a Title/Name is itself one big giant tangle of promises and pledges with no physical form unless pushed into a vulnerable stage.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to deal real damage to the Title, you'd need a way to find out their clauses and how to break them. Sometimes you need to get them to do forbidden acts, sometimes you can do something they are bound to prevent. This generally will strip them of Regalia, and once they have no more Regalia left, you can kill it permanently. More fundamental oaths broken cause more damage, so finding the right linchpin to pull is another viable way to go.<br /> <br /> If you can somehow get them to break a promise made on their True Name, then the Name itself will die. On the other hand, the Titles scatter to the Wyrd, and whatever Fae picks it up is probably going to act in the same way the last one did, so from your perspective, nothing may have changed at all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1516-solarious","name":"Solarious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T03:40:16-07:00","id":1114098,"title":"","content":"Is it just me or does it seem like a True Fae reduced to just it's name have no access to contracts if they are all invested into it's titles. I wish it was clearer what powers remain to a name only True Fae, like can it still shape change and manipulate reality, and if so does it base it on it's name which might not have theme or is it more free form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T05:47:29-07:00","id":1114122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1114098#post1114098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me or does it seem like a True Fae reduced to just it's name have no access to contracts if they are all invested into it's titles. I wish it was clearer what powers remain to a name only True Fae, like can it still shape change and manipulate reality, and if so does it base it on it's name which might not have theme or is it more free form?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say it can still shape reality in Arcadia. It's name might have its own theme","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T12:58:38-07:00","id":1114249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1114098#post1114098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me or does it seem like a True Fae reduced to just it's name have no access to contracts if they are all invested into it's titles. I wish it was clearer what powers remain to a name only True Fae, like can it still shape change and manipulate reality, and if so does it base it on it's name which might not have theme or is it more free form?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would think that varies from Stranger to Stranger based on how much they invested in their Name (dangerous, but wide reaching) versus Titles (safer, but limited in scope).<br /> <br /> I would note the true core of the Fae mechanically are Aspirations, to which they are limited to three, meaning a Fae is only likely to have a cluster of Titles which can be bent towards those Aspirations. That being is seriously defined by what the being wants in a hardcore way. It might have stray Titles which are more atrophied decorations and bartering chips than things that significantly matter to it, but mostly it'd actively pursue more of what its Aspirations are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-10-2017, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T13:33:21-07:00","id":1114256,"title":"","content":"I hadn't even thought about it like that. All of their Titles share the same aspirations and work toward their goals together","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T13:54:25-07:00","id":1114263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1114249#post1114249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would note the true core of the Fae mechanically are Aspirations, to which they are limited to three, meaning a Fae is only likely to have a cluster of Titles which can be bent towards those Aspirations. That being is seriously defined by what the being wants in a hardcore way. It might have stray Titles which are more atrophied decorations and bartering chips than things that significantly matter to it, but mostly it'd actively pursue more of what its Aspirations are.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that changeling-related Aspirations are called out as necessary for and belonging to specific Titles would seem to suggest that the three Aspirations are per encountered manifestation rather than per Fae overall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T15:08:39-07:00","id":1114293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1114098#post1114098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me or does it seem like a True Fae reduced to just it's name have no access to contracts if they are all invested into it's titles. I wish it was clearer what powers remain to a name only True Fae, like can it still shape change and manipulate reality, and if so does it base it on it's name which might not have theme or is it more free form?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A Gentry may have 5 Titles and one Regalia per title. The sixth Regalia may belong to its True Name. So I assume by inference from the write up. Clarification would be good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T15:14:23-07:00","id":1114294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1114263#post1114263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that changeling-related Aspirations are called out as necessary for and belonging to specific Titles would seem to suggest that the three Aspirations are per encountered manifestation rather than per Fae overall.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you mean:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald and Travis Stout</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-true-fae-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\">If the Title is a Keeper, one of its Aspirations should reflect its desire to capture \u2014 or recapture \u2014 a changeling. One Aspiration should always reflect a craving of some kind, something the Title wants to possess more than anything, such as \u201cthe love of a human\u201d or \u201cone million loyal subjects</a>;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Which seems to imply Aspirations may be Title specific, but then there is this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald and Travis Stout</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Character Concept and Titles: </b>A True Fae has three Aspirations just like changelings do. Whenever it fulfills an Aspiration, it gains a Willpower point instead of a Beat, which goes away at the end of the scene if not spent unless it was earned pursuing a craving or a changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which states Aspirations are limited to three per True Fae, and while I am well aware that this is meant to be written in natural language and not technical language, it is less of a stretch that a True Fae has 3 Aprirations as written, and some Titles express different Aspirations to varying degrees than to need to come up with a potential of 15 Aspirations for a True Fae with 5 Titles. At very least it streamlines the process, makes for an interesting clustering of Titles interactions that are held together by a being with 3 Asprirations some of which may be in conflict.<br /> <br /> Imagine This<br /> <br /> <b>Grandmother, Grandmother</b><br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Nurture neglected children, Devour the Damned, Damn those without purpose<br /> <b>Other Titles: </b>Prince of the Pit, Maw of Perdition<br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> The dark whispers in the bunks at night are not dark enough, those changelings that stay until they are adults <i>are </i>sacrificed, but it isn't to another being but rather to the more fiendish Titles of the very Other that raised them.<br /> <br /> I think this conceptually captures the whole concept beautifully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-14-2017, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T17:34:43-07:00","id":1114828,"title":"","content":"How do Charlatans differ from normal True Fae in 2ED?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T21:26:15-07:00","id":1114903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1114828#post1114828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do Charlatans differ from normal True Fae in 2ED?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they are locked in Ironside with only one Title?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-12-2017, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T01:59:25-07:00","id":1114981,"title":"","content":"From a first edition perspective this seems a bit... unfair to players of the Summer Court. The entire theme of the summer court is learning to fight to defend yourself and even to fight back against the True Fae. However this makes it explicitly clear that violently killing a True Fae's seeming human form dosn't do permanent damage. And in general it feels a bit anti-climactic that violence can't permanently hurt the True Fae. If a Summer Courtier manages to defeat a True Fae in single combat that should be the stuff of legends.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the rules binding the True Fae might say that part of the fundamental contracts that define their existence say that if they wish to manifest a physical body outside of Arcadia they must wager a Title or their Name on it's survival. Courts like Summer or South could go further and have as part of their court advantages that if a Gentry wants to take something from them, even in Arcadia itself, they must either delegate the task to a minion or manifest a body or bodies to use as the tool for their taking and wager a Title or Name on that body's survival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-12-2017, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T03:22:22-07:00","id":1115003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1114981#post1114981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a first edition perspective this seems a bit... unfair to players of the Summer Court. The entire theme of the summer court is learning to fight to defend yourself and even to fight back against the True Fae. However this makes it explicitly clear that violently killing a True Fae's seeming human form dosn't do permanent damage. And in general it feels a bit anti-climactic that violence can't permanently hurt the True Fae. If a Summer Courtier manages to defeat a True Fae in single combat that should be the stuff of legends.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>That's why Seasonal Courts are working in alliance</i> - Summer kills nearest True-Fae-as-army going on Freehold. In meantime, Autumn try to find a way to disrupt it's Title. And Winter looks our for <b><i>next</i></b> True Fae interested in the Freehold. Only Spring is partying and politicing in Seasonal Freehold, most of the time.<br /> <br /> Also, in 2E CtL, much more day-to-day enemy are Huntsman - True Fae hunting are to be stuff of chronicle and high Wyrd PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T03:42:09-07:00","id":1115009,"title":"","content":"That's not a counter argument. The setup of the True Fae invalidates charachter concepts that are fit within the themes of Changeling. If a player wants to play a Changeling who's aspiration is to become such a skilled swordsman that they can kill their former keeper in single combat then that's a thematically appropriate charachter and the rules should make it mechanically possible for a skilled and dedicated player to succeed.<br /> <br /> A player who wants their summer courtier to defend the Freehold while the autumn court player finds a way to destroy the Keeper for good is a completely different concept. The fact it works has no bearing on the fact the first concept does not mechanically work. Both concepts are valid, both should be mechanically supported.<br /> <br /> It should be possible to play all four seasonal courts as the hero who strikes the final blow (even Winter who's theme is hiding from the gentry) and it should be possible to play all four seasonal courts as supporting. The autumn court charting a path through the Hedge so that the summer courtiers can walk to the gentry's gate and challenge him to combat should be just as valid as the summer court defending the freehold until the autumn court find a way to use it's bargains against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-12-2017, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T05:44:30-07:00","id":1115049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1114981#post1114981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a first edition perspective this seems a bit... unfair to players of the Summer Court. The entire theme of the summer court is learning to fight to defend yourself and even to fight back against the True Fae. However this makes it explicitly clear that violently killing a True Fae's seeming human form dosn't do permanent damage. And in general it feels a bit anti-climactic that violence can't permanently hurt the True Fae. If a Summer Courtier manages to defeat a True Fae in single combat that should be the stuff of legends.</div> </div> </div> </div> Counter point - tricking a Title into a duel of honor and sealing it, then defeating the Fae is entirely within Summer's wheelhouse. Physical combat is still viable against Loyalists, random hob encounters, and Huntsmen as well. In fact, if we assume the whole use-weapon-against-them thing holds true, physical combat is the ONLY way to put down a Huntsman. And, if you got one of the True Fae breathing down your neck, having someone giving you three weeks breathing room is HUGE. That gives you time to plan, or run, or whatever.<br /> <br /> With all due respect, I'm seeing plenty of room for Summer to do their thing, and in a way that resonates with Changeling: the Lost as a whole. And with the CofD as a whole - its very a common theme in most games that physical combat is NOT the right answer to most antagonists. At least, not physical combat alone. You need banes and bans to fight ephemeral entities; killing them just makes them come back later. Killing humans comes with legal consequences. And so on. Physical combat has never been the universal answer in any gameline. Not even Werewolf or Hunter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115009#post1115009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not a counter argument.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, I do have to agree with Wyrd here. Roleplaying games, as a whole, are cooperative games. There should be coordinated efforts from all members of the motley to finish up a plot, especially one as big as killing a Title. And, nine times out of ten, I see the PC motley made up of various Courts, not just the local combat one. Mystics, combatants, socialites, scouts, criminals, artists/craftsmen, and more. The game shouldn't favor outright combat as a solution, because that's going to make the game into a glorified D&amp;D game. Any solution should really involve working together. Not only because that's how TTRPGs work, but because that's how Changeling, as a whole, works - questions of trust and betrayal are huge huge things. Can you really trust the other courts to get their jobs done? What if the Winter cuts a deal for extra security for themselves and sells others out?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a player wants to play a Changeling who's aspiration is to become such a skilled swordsman that they can kill their former keeper in single combat then that's a thematically appropriate charachter and the rules should make it mechanically possible for a skilled and dedicated player to succeed. </div> </div> </div> A good thing that still exists, then. Just need to tie the Keeper up in pledges so that losing will cause a chain reaction that kills them. Tangled webs of oaths are part and parcel of the game. Everything in the new game comes down to some kind of Pact Magic. Is it any surprise that the game is requiring you to use an oath to permanently stop a Keeper in some way? That's the foundation the entire game is built upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T06:21:13-07:00","id":1115062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115049#post1115049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Counter point - tricking a Title into a duel of honor and sealing it, then defeating the Fae is entirely within Summer's wheelhouse.</div> </div> </div> </div> That sounds like a Spring/Summer or Summer/Autumn teem up to me. Obviously Summer will be good at tricky pledges, they're faeries after all, but if they're good enough to trick a True Fae they're probably specialising in pledgecrafting which isn't Summer's speciality.<br /> <br /> Now if there was a mechanic where a Changeling could challenge someone to a Wyrd enforced duel that could be used to get a True Fae to wager a Name/Title without trickery, then that would be a fitting solution to this issue IMO.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115049#post1115049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roleplaying games, as a whole, are cooperative games. There should be coordinated efforts from all members of the motley to finish up a plot, especially one as big as killing a Title. And, nine times out of ten, I see the PC motley made up of various Courts, not just the local combat one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with everything you say here.<br /> <br /> But &quot;nine times out of ten&quot; means that one time out of ten you'll see an exception, and with a popular game 10% will amount to an awful lot of games. So I think that the rules should be flexible enough to cover that exception.<br /> <br /> Obviously not at the expense of the other nine times. But I don't think saying that a True Fae's core-pledges require them to make a Name/Title vulnerable if it physically incarnates on Earth or the Hedge will have downsides. For one thing, it's completely in the Storyteller's control when, how and if the True Fae appear on Earth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115049#post1115049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The game shouldn't favor outright combat as a solution</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't want to favour outright combat; but I do want to place it on an equal footing to other solutions when it comes to the final climax of the game - which is the natural place to find destroying a Title/Name.<br /> <br /> (As per Rose's request I'm limiting this repose to just the True Fae and not Huntsmen, etc. That said, I think the unique role of the Keeper in every Changeling's backstory means that the giving one court an disadvantage in dealing with the True Fae themselves directly cannot be balanced out by giving them advantages elsewhere)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-12-2017, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T06:44:02-07:00","id":1115068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115062#post1115062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That sounds like a Spring/Summer or Summer/Autumn teem up to me. Obviously Summer will be good at tricky pledges, they're faeries after all, but if they're good enough to trick a True Fae they're probably specialising in pledgecrafting which isn't Summer's speciality.</div> </div> </div> </div> To quote your own post - &quot;It should be possible to play all four seasonal courts as the hero who strikes the final blow (even Winter who's theme is hiding from the gentry) and it should be possible to play all four seasonal courts as supporting.&quot; <br /> <br /> In this case, Summer is the &quot;hero&quot; striking the final blow, and Spring doing the dealing. That's exactly what you said you wanted. Unless what you're actually saying is you want a Summer that can solo a Keeper. At which point, I'm goign to say you're out of luck, no game should allow that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But &quot;nine times out of ten&quot; means that one time out of ten you'll see an exception, and with a popular game 10% will amount to an awful lot of games. So I think that the rules should be flexible enough to cover that exception. </div> </div> </div> Its actually going to be far less than 10%, I was not being literal. Still, the exact number is immaterial. <br /> <br /> The game is more flexible than you give it credit for, because even if everyone is part of the same Court, you're still not going to be all tanky types who specialize in single combats. Summer traditionally does support their own information lines and combat sorcerers. Fleeting Summer was great for a Summer socialite pushing people into making rash bargains. So, unless you have a motley of four carbon-copy heavy-duty fighter types, which I have never seen nor heard of before, you're still going to have all the resources to pull this same scenario off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I don't think saying that a True Fae's title is vulnerable if it physically incarnates on Earth or the Hedge will have many downsides. For one thing, it's completely in the Storyteller's control when, how and if the True Fae appear on Earth. </div> </div> </div> No one is saying anything about the Gentry appearing on earth. They do, and fairly often, since the Keepers do appear in person to carry off new changelings with fair frequency, but I was assuming an Arcadian invasion type scenario.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't want to favour outright combat; but I do want to place it on an equal footing to other solutions when it comes to the final climax of the game - which is the natural place to find destroying a Title/Name. </div> </div> </div> As things stand, you're asking to make combat a superior option than any other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T07:19:10-07:00","id":1115083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115068#post1115068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To quote your own post - &quot;It should be possible to play all four seasonal courts as the hero who strikes the final blow (even Winter who's theme is hiding from the gentry) and it should be possible to play all four seasonal courts as supporting.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I know. I was responding to the fact to you saying it was &quot;entirely within&quot; summer's wheelhouse... I think we're getting sucked into minutiae here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115068#post1115068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Still, the exact number is immaterial.</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115068#post1115068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, unless you have a motley of four carbon-copy heavy-duty fighter types, which I have never seen nor heard of before</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard of it. I've played in a game where the Storyteller pitched it as a wild hunt through the hedge so we all created hunters. I've also played play by post games where every charachter was essentially independent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115068#post1115068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one is saying anything about the Gentry appearing on earth.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually I was. Back in my first post on this thread I made two suggestions: The first is that to physically manifest a body outside of Arcadia a True Fae must use a Title/Name as collateral against their survival as agreed upon in the core oaths that allow the gentry to exist.<br /> <br /> The second was that if, and only if, the True Fae wished to take something from a Summer Courtier while they're in Arcadia they must either get a minion to do it (thus drastically limiting their power) or they must do so by manifesting a body with a Title at risk if they're killed - as per the court's agreement with Summer. (The idea was that other courts get their own advantages)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115068#post1115068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As things stand, you're asking to make combat a superior option than any other.</div> </div> </div> </div>in what way?<br /> <br /> Currently a tricky pledge can destroy a Title without combat; but combat cannot destroy a Title without a tricky pledge. I want both techniques to be mechanically possible in isolation.<br /> <br /> My ideal situation would be to maximise the Storyteller's flexibility in the tasks they may set players to destroy a Name/Title. If they end up with a mixed motley they can design challenges that require all the players to work together. If they end up with a very specialised motley (or are giving each player a solo session against their own keeper) they can fine tune the challenge to that character's skill set.<br /> <br /> But seriously. How do you think I'm trying to make combat superior? Because that is not my intent, so either there's a misunderstanding somewhere or a flaw in my suggestions that you see but haven't explicitly stated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-12-2017, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T07:34:15-07:00","id":1115086,"title":"","content":"This conversation is a symposium worthy of the great College of Worms. &lt;3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T07:35:54-07:00","id":1115087,"title":"","content":"Ironically when I played a Changeling charachter who was a perfect fit for the college of worms she refused to join because she was too vain to accept the Entitlement's skin condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-12-2017, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T08:33:10-07:00","id":1115101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115062#post1115062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That sounds like a Spring/Summer or Summer/Autumn teem up to me. Obviously Summer will be good at tricky pledges, they're faeries after all, but if they're good enough to trick a True Fae they're probably specialising in pledgecrafting which isn't Summer's speciality.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one thing I've noticed when role-playing beings more intelligent than I, critical re-evaluation and taking more time to make plans/contingencies/decisions than the being would need to do the same can simulate being smarter. Intelligence after all can be considered processing power to problem solve. There is an axiom &quot;writing is rewriting&quot; which feels applicable, what appears to be the result of a flash of genius and brilliance can instead and likely is the result of a hardworking long-slow-low-burn instead.<br /> <br /> A Summer Courtier who spends their whole free life focused on training to kill a single True Fae, mastering weapons, violent brutal Contracts, and specifically the weaknesses of his particular quarry. He wouldn't master pledgesmithing in general, like an Autumn Courtier, but he'd be writing and rewriting, and memorizing pledges that'd work against this one most important foe, which can be represented with a single Skill Specialty (Trap X to their doom.) and two 1 dot merits (Area of Expertise, and Interdisciplinary Specialty for the aforementioned Specialty) and the resulting Plan equipment bonus. That is very cheap point wise for the massive amount of flavor it adds to the character concept.<br /> <br /> That doesn't really take too much away from the normal Summer specialty and if anything enhances it in a special situation. This would be particularly valuable if a specific Keeper had an interest in the area where the freehold is, and multiple members of that Freehold were held captive by that Keeper.<br /> <br /> As said before, killing a True Fae is an entire Chronicle in and of itself, not a fleeting adventure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-12-2017, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T09:48:12-07:00","id":1115120,"title":"","content":"It seems really weird also to say that the Summer Court's shtick is diminished or disadvantaged because just physically beating a gentry manifestation isn't enough to permanently end them. The role of the Summer Court against their former captors and their kin has never been summed up by fighting their avatars, even in First Edition. Their methods heavily invole fighting back directly and bringing the battle to the fae and their machinations, but that doesn't mean they're all focused on facing fae actors or that it's even what they do most. (It also logically couldn't be, because the Others acting on the Ironside in such a form was meant to be rare and extremely weighty, not a casual means to their ends.)<br /> <br /> Implying that the temporary banishment of a title by defeating its humanoid manifestation in combat can't be incredibly significant on its own also sounds like dropping the ball. Your initial critique, KingsRaven, sounds like it's dealing in some fairly exaggerated suggestions, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-12-2017, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T09:54:52-07:00","id":1115128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115083#post1115083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> in what way?<br /> <br /> Currently a tricky pledge can destroy a Title without combat; but combat cannot destroy a Title without a tricky pledge. I want both techniques to be mechanically possible in isolation.</div> </div> </div> </div> Because you can't actually get a &quot;tricky pledge&quot; of any kind in isolation. You need leverage - quite possibly involving stealing the physical Regalia, and good luck doing that alone - to bring a Keeper to the bargaining table in the first place! Also, there are multiple kinds of pledges, how you might angle things to a pledge, the nature of the Keeper in question, and more. Ancient beings with alien minds and god-like power have no reason to pledge their Names or Titles on anything unless you force them to somehow. You are severely underestimating how hard getting a &quot;tricky pledge&quot; is. <br /> <br /> Because the entire game revolves around pledge, pacts, bargains, oaths, vows and whatever other word you want for a mystical bargain. Everyone does it. When you join a court. When you learn a Contract. When you make a motley. When you visit with goblins. Pledgecraft is a major part of the game. Trying to say that combat and pledges should be on the same level is like saying that combat and magic should be on the same level in Mage. Or that Prometheans should be able to combat their way to the New Dawn. Combat has its place in those games, but in each case, its working with the themes, not proposing itself as an alternative.<br /> <br /> Because Changeling is a game where the protagonists are fae, and are expected to think and act like fae. <br /> <br /> Because &quot;tricky pledge&quot; isn't one thing. Its something that can be done through social-fu, through mystic study, through eavesdropping on monologging villains, and more. They all have different approaches and means of addressing this situation. Putting combat on par with all of that, combined? That's like saying that combat should be equal to espionage in a Demon game. That doesn't make sense. <br /> <br /> Because the game places a fair amount of emphasis on duels and sworn enemies, and there are ancient pacts that revolve around duels, especially if you hold them in the Hedge or Arcadia proper, not Ironside. The Wyrd witnesses them and seals it and enforces it. <br /> <br /> Because combat &quot;in isolation&quot; is never an answer for the big bads. Strix and elders don't go down from combat - they go down from using banes and maneuvering things to your advantage, alying the ground work. Major spirits and idigam need research to find their weaknesses. Mage is all about the research and information, fighting lies with Truth and Knowledge. Promethean's &quot;big bad&quot; are firestorms. Demons can't just combat the God Machine; they're spies, and need to espionage their way through. Sin-Eaters can't just fight Keroberus - they need to make use of the Old Laws.<br /> <br /> Because when you start giving villains HP tracks that PCs can just punch to make the villain go away, that's exactly what happens, and the game suffers for it, and you make a being of godlike power look... dumb. It happened a lot in 1e before equinox roads, where players saw Gentry as nothing more than high level changelings, and could easily handle them. Not scary at all. Its the whole idea that as soon as you stat something, you get players who try to beat that something, and that's not the theme I imagine changeling is going for.<br /> <br /> I could go on. There's a million things going on here that puts a lot of askance on trying to punch out Cthulhu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T10:05:17-07:00","id":1115131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115120#post1115120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems really weird also to say that the Summer Court's shtick is diminished or disadvantaged because just physically beating a gentry manifestation isn't enough to permanently end them. The role of the Summer Court against their former captors and their kin has never been summed up by fighting their avatars, even in First Edition. Their methods heavily invole fighting back directly and bringing the battle to the fae and their machinations, but that doesn't mean they're all focused on facing fae actors or that it's even what they do most. (It also logically couldn't be, because the Others acting on the Ironside in such a form was meant to be rare and extremely weighty, not a casual means to their ends.)<br /> <br /> Implying that the temporary banishment of a title by defeating its humanoid manifestation in combat can't be incredibly significant on its own also sounds like dropping the ball. Your initial critique, KingsRaven, sounds like it's dealing in some fairly exaggerated suggestions, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Summer is War. And war comes in many flavors. Perhaps a Sun Tzunian Summer courtier creates a strategy beyond which even a Gentry could hope to outwit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T11:56:41-07:00","id":1115172,"title":"","content":"I want to be surprised that there's a gross misunderstanding about the way Summer works or even how Changeling, a game about faeries, works....but this has unfortunately become par for the course.<br /> <br /> War for Summer was never a one dimensional subject. Summer had sorcerers and thieves and accountants and riddle makers(who were probably also accountants) and everything of the sort. The difference is that the spectrum of activity was geared towards uncompromising aggression towards the Strangers, where as Autumn** was all about that critical hinge point that exists in compromise, the power that comes from being afraid, the power that comes from being at the center of pledges. Summer plays chess with the fae on six or seven dimensions, maybe more, but it's all about taking down that king-and as any mediocre chess player knows, you can't rely one one type of &quot;movement&quot; to win the game.<br /> <br /> Does that mean physical combat is never the answer? The whole lore of faerie tales says that's not the case, and Changeling facilitates it. But just as often, it's a matter of setting up that combat. You can't beat the Moon King with any sword, you need the Sword Unbreakable*. The battle can't happen anywhere, the Dark Lord must die on the hollow of bones he was born in. Physical combat can't just be physical combat, it has to have gravitas, meaning, it must be an actualization. This is how combat has <i>always</i> worked in faerie tales-the ones worth reading, anyways.<br /> <br /> Final thing: When a 10% chance is mentioned that a Character who has the Aspiration of defeating a Stranger by taking their head off will be let down, that's....not the fault of the game. The game gives you the tools to make that happen. If it does happen, it's because the Storyteller is a rank dick(and probably the rest of the players, if they aren't confronting said Storyteller).<br /> <br /> Broaden your reading, sharpen your understanding. I know some people are tired of me saying that, but Changeling is <i>not</i> a game you can just charge your thoughts at it straight on. The world of the fae is sideways to expectation and will gladly trip and devour any who try.<br /> <br /> *Poor reference, I know, but follow me here.<br /> **As the <i>other</i> major war-like faction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-12-2017, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T12:32:32-07:00","id":1115192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115128#post1115128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because when you start giving villains HP tracks that PCs can just punch to make the villain go away, that's exactly what happens, and the game suffers for it, and you make a being of godlike power look... dumb. It happened a lot in 1e before equinox roads, where players saw Gentry as nothing more than high level changelings, and could easily handle them. Not scary at all. Its the whole idea that as soon as you stat something, you get players who try to beat that something, and that's not the theme I imagine changeling is going for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lets start with this one. My philosophy is that a splat is a contract (pun intended) between the designers and the players. If you have a court who's write up says &quot;these guys like to fight&quot; then fighting must be applicable to the games core conflicts, including the changeling and it's Keeper. You could of course redesign the summer court to put less focus on combat, but since we don't know Rose's take I'm going by their 1E incarnation.<br /> <br /> And for the record. I see nothing wrong with giving villains HP tracks. Some players like a villain that they can punch, designing mechanics flexible enough to provide for those players and also provide for players who like their villains to be beyond violence. Plus plenty of faerie tale villains were ultimately defeated by violence. The gentry's promise based existence is tailor made for this kind of flexibility, as there can be all sorts of conditions and loopholes that sate that a gentry's mechanics work one way in one situation but another way in another situation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Where I fundamentally disagree with you, is not your interpretation of the True Fae and their themes; but your insistence that there is a correct interpretation. You say it &quot;looks dumb&quot; if you can punch a godlike being, but dumb is in the eye of the beholder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115128#post1115128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because you can't actually get a &quot;tricky pledge&quot; of any kind in isolation.</div> </div> </div> </div> Counterpoint. This is exactly what Puss in Boots did, he walked into the ogre's lair with no advantages or hidden aces and beat the ogre with nothing but his wit. Granted the ogre was as dumb as a bag of rocks, but the idea of a charachter who finds the courage to face their darkest fear, alone, without weapons or advantages, and defeats them with nothing but their wits and their words is absolutely epic and awesome (e.g. most of Doctor Who) so I'd be very disappointed if the mechanics forbade it by making the Gentry unbeatable in a game of wits without a hidden advantage.<br /> <br /> Rumpelstiltskin would be another example of an easily acquired pledge in a classic faerie tale. I have absolutely no idea why a Gentry would offer a pledge that could lead to their destruction with no discernable advantage from making it - but IMO if Rumpelstiltskin did it then it's automatically a valid thing for a True Fae to do. Even if it would take some very good storytelling to not make it look like a Deus Ex Machnia in the player's favour.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115128#post1115128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pledgecraft is a major part of the game. Trying to say that combat and pledges should be on the same level is like saying that combat and magic should be on the same level in Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div> In Mage combat is a form of magic, in that blasting someone with magic is a valid alternative to a gun. Now if Changeling could make combat a form of pledgecraft, allowing the summer court to bind a Keeper to a pledge with exceptional swordplay or gunplay then that would resolve the issue. (and be all round awesome). I have no idea how that could work though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115128#post1115128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Changeling is a game where the protagonists are fae, and are expected to think and act like fae.</div> </div> </div> </div> By definition, your Y-Splats philosophy is a valid way for the protagonists to think. The summer court like directness.<br /> <br /> Anyway that's enough for now. I need to reply to others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115120#post1115120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems really weird also to say that the Summer Court's shtick is diminished or disadvantaged because just physically beating a gentry manifestation isn't enough to permanently end them. The role of the Summer Court against their former captors and their kin has never been summed up by fighting their avatars, even in First Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div> Please don't assume I'm thinking the Summer Court are only or exclusively about fighting. Rather I'm saying that the write up and mechanics of the summer court are very clearly saying to players that combat focused characters are supported in changeling. For example The Mantle has three bonuses that are applicable in physical combat, and none that a firebrand lawyer could.<br /> <br /> And if you have a splat for combat characters I believe that the rest of the game should allow combat approach to work. This is especially true in the most personal and fundamental conflict in all of Changeling. The changeling vs their keeper.<br /> <br /> To use Mage as an example. It also had a splat that was promised players the ability to play combat characters; and when we get to the climax Imperial Mysteries had plenty of support for achieving archmastery through a victory in battle; and further support for progressing to ascension itself through combat (since Omens were incredibly customisable)<br /> <br /> (As for why I'm talking only about fighting Keepers and not other things; as I've said before, this thread is about Keepers)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115172#post1115172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to be surprised that there's a gross misunderstanding about the way Summer works or even how Changeling, a game about faeries, works....but this has unfortunately become par for the course.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think my reply to YeOfLittleFaith doubles here.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that Summer is <u>only</u> includes war or physical combat. I'm saying that summer <u>includes</u> war and physical combat (in an important central role). A summer court firebrand lawyer who wins court cases through uncompromising aggression is definitely a valid summer concept; and it's clear that guy could use his lawyer skills to pledgecraft against a gentry and thus threaten a Title/Name.<br /> <br /> But a backstreet brawler is also a valid summer court concept; and that guy should also be able to use his schtick in a climatic final confrontation against his keeper to threaten a Title/Name.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115172#post1115172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physical combat can't just be physical combat, it has to have gravitas, meaning, it must be an actualization. This is how combat has <i>always</i> worked in faerie tales-the ones worth reading, anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div> No disagreement from me. Actually I think we're agreeing on most things.<br /> <br /> But that gravitas and meaning can come internally from the charachter, especially when the relationship between the combatants is as intimate as the relationship between Changeling and Keeper.<br /> <br /> Sometimes you need to go on an epic quest to find the sword unbrakable. Sometimes you just need to spend a Chronicle transforming yourself from a terrified slave into someone with the emotional and physical strength to look your Keeper in the eye and say &quot;I'm ready, lets fight!&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-12-2017, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T13:48:43-07:00","id":1115234,"title":"","content":"Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a> do let us know if this goes on too long. I know these discussions have before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T16:14:30-07:00","id":1115286,"title":"","content":"Hey guys... given how myriad the Strangers are, I say it's not too far-fetched to assume there really is a Title out there who can only be beaten by an honorable duel or on a glorious battlefield. Then the theoretical and highly unrealistic one-trick pony who only joined the Summer Court because all they can do is brawl and are unable to come up with martial strategies and alternative warfare can have a chance to shine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T19:22:02-07:00","id":1115338,"title":"","content":"I don't really follow the line of thought. In any edition, it doesn't make much sense to have a changeling focus on becoming skilled with the sword unless there is some meaning to the effort. If the meaning is focused on the Keeper then sword fighting must be relevant to the Keeper in some way. The Keeper is created to match the changeling. I wouldn't expect the swordsman's Keeper to be a scientist working at the center of a maze full of traps. How does it work out in 2e?<br /> <br /> Seems to me a Keeper is destroyed by forcing it to break the Contract that binds its existence. That might be telling a unique story, winning a fair duel, navigating a maze, or evading capture for a certain amount of time within a designated area. Some work for combat heavy types while others do not. Works out equally for every type of character. Then there are loopholes to exploit that are easy for anyone but getting the chance is the trick. Pulling a sword from a stone might require defeating the guardian, a master swordsman.<br /> <br /> I don't think they are invalidating character concepts with this new approach. I do think they are trying to avoid the option of using more dakka. If one changeling can kill a True Fae by dealing damage by learning a few (perhaps more than a few) skills then 5 or 10 changelings could do the same without the need for dedication. I think they want the concept created to defeat a Keeper to be made specifically to defeat that Keeper because if someone wants to focus their character that much they should be rewarded with &quot;Great shot, kid. That was one in a million.&quot; rather than you filled up the last health box now figure out what to do with the rest of your life.<br /> <br /> The thing about 2e Keepers is sometimes they come back. I actually can see a swordsman concept, which is a bit odd as choices go for general play, as a concept that is, when created with purpose, supported better in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T06:38:00-07:00","id":1115503,"title":"","content":"I'm not really feeling the use-Name-against the True Fae thing. Like, if we're talking about forging Contracts with Arcadia itself to do everything, why is simply knowing the name going to grant you advantages against them? I don't understand the logic behind it. Everything in changeling should be coming down to Contracts. That's why Iron is a fae bane - a broken Contract. Where does the whole inscribing-a-name-on-a-weapon come from? Getting exceptional successes on Contracts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T08:38:53-07:00","id":1115543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115503#post1115503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not really feeling the use-Name-against the True Fae thing. Like, if we're talking about forging Contracts with Arcadia itself to do everything, why is simply knowing the name going to grant you advantages against them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing the name and speaking it lets you cut past the rest of the word-bonds empowering a Fae manifestation to strike at its core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why Iron is a fae bane - a broken Contract. </div> </div> </div>That's one theory among many, not a known fact; all the evidence in support of it applies equally well to other forms of &quot;the True Fae, entities who engage with all of reality through agreements, agreed to some deal whose conditions led to their vulnerability to iron.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where does the whole inscribing-a-name-on-a-weapon come from? </div> </div> </div>I'm seeing nothing about inscription anywhere in the blog or this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T10:30:14-07:00","id":1115579,"title":"","content":"The impression I got was a True Fae is its Name, so it would be like using a diamond to cut another diamond. They have a vibe like Mr. Mxyptlk from Superman, I don't think such beings have an actual physical presence. They manifest their power in a way that allows them to interact with lesser beings. A True Fae can't defend against itself without limiting its own power so... it works out that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T11:39:44-07:00","id":1115614,"title":"","content":"So True Fae have a Name at their core and up to five Titles. Each Title can Manefest X times/ways. <br /> <br /> What if it's deeper than that? What if a True True Fe consists of up to five names, each with up to five titles, with up to x manifestations. <br /> <br /> But actually, it gets further, The Wyrd several True Fae Manifestations, each with up to five names, with up to five titles, with up to x manifestations. <br /> <br /> This is just theory crafting here but what if the Wyrd, who is in essence twisting pacts and pledges that intersect like threads and entwine like a spiderweb or a dream catcher, is the actual &quot;enemy&quot;. The Wyrd is the Spider and the Trap catching stories, dreams, and ideas. If changelings still become Fae as the end game, they just get obsorbed and claimed by the Wyrd. <br /> <br /> Just an idea for a possibly very long Chronicle with the end result being no more Fae. Killing the Wyrd. Just thinking out loud here I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T13:44:55-07:00","id":1115658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115614#post1115614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So True Fae have a Name at their core and up to five Titles. Each Title can Manefest X times/ways.<br /> <br /> What if it's deeper than that? What if a True True Fe consists of up to five names, each with up to five titles, with up to x manifestations.<br /> <br /> But actually, it gets further, The Wyrd several True Fae Manifestations, each with up to five names, with up to five titles, with up to x manifestations.<br /> <br /> This is just theory crafting here but what if the Wyrd, who is in essence twisting pacts and pledges that intersect like threads and entwine like a spiderweb or a dream catcher, is the actual &quot;enemy&quot;. The Wyrd is the Spider and the Trap catching stories, dreams, and ideas. If changelings still become Fae as the end game, they just get obsorbed and claimed by the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Just an idea for a possibly very long Chronicle with the end result being no more Fae. Killing the Wyrd. Just thinking out loud here I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a Bridge-Burner Chronicle","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T04:41:45-07:00","id":1115879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115128#post1115128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Because you can't actually get a &quot;tricky pledge&quot; of any kind in isolation. You need leverage - quite possibly involving stealing the physical Regalia, and good luck doing that alone - to bring a Keeper to the bargaining table in the first place! Also, there are multiple kinds of pledges, how you might angle things to a pledge, the nature of the Keeper in question, and more. Ancient beings with alien minds and god-like power have no reason to pledge their Names or Titles on anything unless you force them to somehow. You are severely underestimating how hard getting a &quot;tricky pledge&quot; is.<br /> <br /> Because the entire game revolves around pledge, pacts, bargains, oaths, vows and whatever other word you want for a mystical bargain. Everyone does it. When you join a court. When you learn a Contract. When you make a motley. When you visit with goblins. Pledgecraft is a major part of the game. Trying to say that combat and pledges should be on the same level is like saying that combat and magic should be on the same level in Mage. Or that Prometheans should be able to combat their way to the New Dawn. Combat has its place in those games, but in each case, its working with the themes, not proposing itself as an alternative.<br /> <br /> Because Changeling is a game where the protagonists are fae, and are expected to think and act like fae.<br /> <br /> Because &quot;tricky pledge&quot; isn't one thing. Its something that can be done through social-fu, through mystic study, through eavesdropping on monologging villains, and more. They all have different approaches and means of addressing this situation. Putting combat on par with all of that, combined? That's like saying that combat should be equal to espionage in a Demon game. That doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> Because the game places a fair amount of emphasis on duels and sworn enemies, and there are ancient pacts that revolve around duels, especially if you hold them in the Hedge or Arcadia proper, not Ironside. The Wyrd witnesses them and seals it and enforces it.<br /> <br /> Because combat &quot;in isolation&quot; is never an answer for the big bads. Strix and elders don't go down from combat - they go down from using banes and maneuvering things to your advantage, alying the ground work. Major spirits and idigam need research to find their weaknesses. Mage is all about the research and information, fighting lies with Truth and Knowledge. Promethean's &quot;big bad&quot; are firestorms. Demons can't just combat the God Machine; they're spies, and need to espionage their way through. Sin-Eaters can't just fight Keroberus - they need to make use of the Old Laws.<br /> <br /> Because when you start giving villains HP tracks that PCs can just punch to make the villain go away, that's exactly what happens, and the game suffers for it, and you make a being of godlike power look... dumb. It happened a lot in 1e before equinox roads, where players saw Gentry as nothing more than high level changelings, and could easily handle them. Not scary at all. Its the whole idea that as soon as you stat something, you get players who try to beat that something, and that's not the theme I imagine changeling is going for.<br /> <br /> I could go on. There's a million things going on here that puts a lot of askance on trying to punch out Cthulhu.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u00b4m thinking in <b><i>Little Nightmares</i></b>: the story of a young girl (Six) kidnapped and trapped in a big, weird submarine (the Maw) where a mysterious witch (The Geisha) plans to use her and the other captured kids to feed her abominable yet upper class &quot;guests&quot;. Six\u00b4s Durance is a journey where she <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> evades or kill her Keeper \u00b4s enforcers ( Janitor, Twins, etc... all loyal hobgoblins) until she arrives the Geisha\u00b4s private room, learns her bane (her own reflection in a mirror), defeat her, and devours the witch Regalia/Title, becoming a True Fae herself.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-jQDyIp0aSw\" data-code=\"-jQDyIp0aSw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/-jQDyIp0aSw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T17:36:26-07:00","id":1116172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1111834-the-true-fae-new-changeling-second-edition-preview?p=1115579#post1115579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The impression I got was a True Fae is its Name, so it would be like using a diamond to cut another diamond. They have a vibe like Mr. Mxyptlk from Superman, I don't think such beings have an actual physical presence. They manifest their power in a way that allows them to interact with lesser beings. A True Fae can't defend against itself without limiting its own power so... it works out that way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mxyzptlk is a 5th dimensional being. He probably does have a physical presence, but we are incapable of perceiving it unless he chooses to announce himself.<br /> <br /> I forgot where I found it, but there's a video on youtube that explains the physical world appears dramatically different from the perspective of 1 and 2 dimensional beings than it does to us. Abilities that seem completely ordinary and rational from our point of view might be mistaken for godly powers when presented to a being who doesn't exist in the same dimensional plane as us.<br /> <br /> So by that extension, Mr. Mxyzptlk's ability to warp reality may have a perfectly scientific explanation where he comes from, but lesser evolved beings like us attribute it to magic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T18:00:04-07:00","id":1116178,"title":"","content":"I meant flesh and blood. Mxy has a physical presence in the same way light or wind does, but depending on what the 4th and 5th dimensions are for him, his body could be an avatar or mental projection used to deal with 3 dimensional beings, almost like some Supernal being. A higher dimensional being exists or doesn't exist from the perceptions of a lower dimensional being and would appear irrational (mathematics) without the ability to downgrade to a lower dimensional state, a projection like a map. Use another example if you want. The point is True Fae are not precisely their manifestations, but that is the means by which one interacts with the True Fae. The Name is a name and all that it represents. Titles are like syllables of a name or more precisely the characters that make up the syllables. The existence of True Fae is bound up in Contracts rather than the material of a manifestation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T11:23:38-07:00","id":1120426,"title":"","content":"Actually, I think of the True Fae as being closer to a much newer cosmic being (in the real world), the First Firmament.<br /> <br /> Those it corrupts have different minds and powers than it, but the same core motive of destroying the universe and replacing it with itself. It also fits the personality, as the FF is essentially a super-divine brat throwing a tantrum that it made people rather than toys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}